# console.db 及其全部伴生文件——本机数据，一律不进 git（2026-08-29 起）。
#
# 在此之前 console.db 是被跟踪的，理由是"它装着 run / schedule / schema 这些真实
# 数据"。那个理由站不住：一个**正在被写入的 SQLite 文件**当源码管，代价是反复付
# 出的，而收益只覆盖其中一部分数据。实际付出过的代价：
#   - 2026-08-27 注册表整个被清空——提交了带活跃 WAL 的半程快照，checkout 时用它
#     覆写主库，得到一个自相矛盾的数据库。
#   - 2026-08-29 一台机器 pull 下来 Book=0 / Schema=0，看起来像装坏了，实际是上游
#     把 reset 后的空库提交了上去。
#   - 多机之间必然冲突：二进制文件 git 合不了，pull 要么被拒、要么直接覆盖掉那台
#     机器的 run 历史。
#
# 而这些数据里，真正需要跨机共享的那部分本来就能重建：
#   Schema（契约注册表） ← node scripts/register-schemas.mjs（幂等）
#   Book（playbook 索引）← POST /api/books/rescan
# 剩下的 Run / StepRun / SchemaRecord 是本机执行历史与产出，本就不该跨机同步。
# register-schemas.mjs 的文件头一直是这么定位自己的："注册表才是真相源，那些
# .schema.json 是最初导入的存档，留着是为了让空库能被 seed"。
#
# 后果，写在这里而不是让人自己撞上：一个全新 clone **没有** console.db，
# `pnpm start` 会被 backend.sh 的 ensure_console_db 拦下并要求先跑 `pnpm init`
# （它用 prisma migrate deploy 建库）。这是刻意的——建库是一个明确的步骤，不该
# 由 start 命令背着人做。
/resource/db/console.db
/resource/db/console.db-wal
/resource/db/console.db-shm
# `-journal` belongs to the same class and was missed until 2026-08-29, by which
# point a 53KB one had been committed. It is the ROLLBACK journal — the
# pre-WAL mechanism — and it appears whenever something opens the database in
# `delete` / `persist` / `truncate` journal mode, which the prisma CLI does
# during `migrate` even though the application runs in WAL. Same hazard as the
# two above and one worse property: a journal whose header is still intact is
# a HOT journal, and SQLite rolls the database back to it on the next open.
# Checking one out next to a `console.db` it does not match is how a clone gets
# a database nobody wrote.
/resource/db/console.db-journal
# Belt and braces for the same class under any name the tooling picks. Matched
# on the SUFFIX, not on a `.db` stem: the companions of a renamed database are
# named after whatever it was renamed to (`console.db.corrupt.<ts>-shm`), and a
# `*.db-shm` pattern silently misses every one of them.
/resource/db/*-journal
/resource/db/*-wal
/resource/db/*-shm

# Local WeClaw recipient configuration
packages/weclaw/config/user.json

# Run-produced files that couldn't fit a schema DB column (records.service.ts).
# Unlike resource/uploads/ (small, user-picked, committed), records/ holds
# whatever a run's own output produces — can be large, is regenerated by
# re-running the book, not meant to live in git history. Anchored with a
# leading slash on purpose: an unanchored `records/` would ALSO match
# packages/console/src/records/ (the source dir this task adds), which is the
# exact mistake .agent/learn.md records for 2026-08-25's `uploads/` incident.
/resource/records/


# Build output — generated on `pnpm build`, never committed.
packages/console/dist-web/
*.tsbuildinfo

